  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ OKOA-Girls Voice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant applied by OKOA New generation aims to support the project to improve the sexual and reproductive health, rights and well-being of vulnerable adolescent girls in Arusha. At the end of implementation, the project intends to achieve the followingwhich include but are not limited to: young girls are empowered to increase their knowledge, information and confidence in decision-making over their sexual reproductive health rights and gender equality.  Improved income and economic status of young girls through sustainable business and entrepreneurship activities.  Increased support from government, families, households, and communities to create anenabling environment for promoting girls&#x2019; reproductive health rights and economic status.
Furthermore,this project intends to empower young girls in family planning, gender and sexual reproductive health and education to increase their knowledge, levels of confidence and decision-making over their sexual reproductive health and rights aspect. The projectwill also establish adolescent girls and young women groups and empower them with entrepreneurship and business skills, economic opportunities, and access to finance, markets and technical services to scale up their businesses.

In order to achieve theintended results, the project aims to implement thefollowing activities:
1. Conduct Project inception meeting with Local Government leader, Community Health Workers, School leaders, key stakeholders including Traditional leaders, value chain actors to address the project objective and creating road map for project implementation.
2. Conduct Identification, formulation of self-help groups for out of school AGYW and school clubs that will participate in the project implementation at ward level.
3. Conduct training to out of school young girls&#x2019; groups and school clubs on gender, life skills, sexual reproductive health and social behavior change communication (SBCC) to increase confidence on decision making over their sexual reproductive health rights and gender equality.
4. Conduct training on business and entrepreneurship skills to out of school Adolescent Girls Young Women groups to improve their income, productivity and wellbeing.
5. Creation and distribution of IEC Materials for awareness raising and advocacy of adolescent girls and young women sexual reproductive health and economic empowerment.
6. Conducting site mentorship, coaching and support supervision to out of school young girls&#x2019; groups and school clubs.
7. Attend VOICE Tanzania programmatic and thematic Linking and Learning events</narrative>
  </description>
